{#-
  The persistence rule of registry/qyl/policy.yaml as a runtime table, in the stable package. The
  span views and the qyl collector's catalog read this one table, so a test can
  never assert a key that ingest drops. Explicit key/prefix denials precede the finite
  captured-field rule. Other keys use the token rule, which token-exempt and vendor keys skip.
  policy.token_exempt holds the annotated keys and the registry enum keys that contain a denied
  token, which scripts/generate.sh adds from the resolved registry.
-#}
